    costImpact: [
      `Robeson's politics cost him money, audience, travel, and public reputation. Passport revocation isolated him internationally. Blacklisting damaged his career in the United States. Friends, venues, and institutions sometimes retreated because association with him carried risk.`,
      `His impact was global. Robeson linked Black freedom to labor rights, anti-fascism, and anti-colonial struggles before those connections were widely accepted in mainstream U.S. culture. He also left a warning about how a government can punish dissent through administrative power, not only prison walls.`
    ],
    whyItMattersToday: [
      `Paul Robeson matters today because artists, athletes, and scholars are still told that political speech makes them ungrateful, divisive, or dangerous. Robeson shows that the demand for silence is often strongest when a public figure connects racism at home to power abroad.`,
      `His story also asks readers to think beyond simple patriotism tests. Robeson criticized the United States because he believed Black people, workers, and colonized people deserved freedom. Whether one agrees with every political judgment he made, the punishment he faced reveals how fragile civil liberties can become under fear.`,
      `The fuller lesson is that a voice can be beautiful and threatening at the same time. Robeson's voice threatened power because he used it for more than applause.`
    ],
